        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How much is a NordicTrack treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              At Black Friday 2026 prices, about $1,599 for the T Series 10 or Commercial 1250, $1,999 for the Commercial 1750, $2,299 for the 2450, and $2,699 to $2,999 for the X16 and X24 incline trainers. NordicTrack's list prices run from $1,999 for the 1250 to $4,299 for the X24 (checked November 2026).
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much does the NordicTrack Commercial 1750 cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              NordicTrack's US store listed it at $2,499 on 21 November 2026, and the Black Friday price we saw at a specialty retailer was $1,999. NordicTrack itself sold it at $1,999.99 in October, so about $2,000 is its usual selling price. Add $396 a year for iFIT Pro if you will use the classes.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is iFIT per month on a NordicTrack?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              iFIT Pro, the plan for NordicTrack machines with a built-in touchscreen, is $39 a month or $396 a year and covers up to five users. iFIT Train is $15 a month or $144 a year but is designed for phones, tablets and equipment without a built-in screen (checked November 2026).
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the cheapest NordicTrack treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Among NordicTrack's own range, the T Series 10 at about $1,599 is the cheapest with a touchscreen this month. Retailer-only models such as the T 6.5 S and T Series 5 Starter cost less; Best Buy's NordicTrack Black Friday prices started at $445.75. A used NordicTrack has a median asking price of about $450.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does NordicTrack include delivery and assembly?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              NordicTrack advertises free shipping, which is threshold delivery: the machine arrives unassembled outside your door. Room of choice delivery and white glove delivery with assembly are offered as upgrades, priced once you enter your ZIP code. Delivery takes 10 to 14 business days according to NordicTrack.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty comes with a NordicTrack treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              NordicTrack's product pages list a 10-year frame, 2-year parts and 1-year labor warranty as standard. The Commercial 1750, 2450, X16 and X24 pages also advertise a lifetime motor warranty; the T Series 10 page describes a 2-year motor warranty. A 3-year extended warranty is offered at checkout.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is it cheaper to buy a NordicTrack at Costco or direct?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It depends on the model and the week, and Costco's pages blocked our price check this month. Warehouse clubs often sell club-specific model numbers, so compare the screen, motor and warranty as well as the price. Direct purchases get NordicTrack's $100 off when you add a prepaid iFIT Pro year.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
